{{also|engravé}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|ingrave}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|eɪv|lang=en}}

===Etymology 1===
From earlier {{term|ingrave|lang=en}}, equivalent to {{prefix|en|grave|gloss2=to carve, engrave|lang=en|nocat=1}}. More at {{l|en|grave}}.

====Verb====
{{en-verb|engrav}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[carve]] text or symbols into (something), usually for the purposes of identification or art.
#: {{ux|en|He '''engraved''' the plaque with his name.}}
#* {{RQ:Chmbrs YngrSt|VIII}}
#*: Elbows almost touching they leaned at ease, idly reading the almost obliterated lines '''engraved''' there. &para; {{nowrap|"I never}} understood it," she observed, lightly scornful. "What occult meaning has a sun-dial for the spooney? ''I'm'' sure I don't want to read riddles in a strange gentleman's optics."
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To carve (something) into a material.
#: {{ux|en|He '''engraved''' his name.}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{sense|carve (text or symbols) into}} [[carve]], [[etch]], [[inscribe]]

